{"name":"Alabaster","hex":"#f3e7db","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Alabaster","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Shelby County, Alabama, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Alabaster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alabaster","blocks":[{"text":"Alabaster is a soft rock used for carvings and as a source of plaster powder. Archaeologists, geologists, and the stone industry have different definitions for the word alabaster. In archaeology, the term alabaster includes objects and artefacts made from two different minerals: (i) the fine-grained, massive type of gypsum, and (ii) the fine-grained, banded type of calcite."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Lioness_Bast_cosmetic_jar_83d40m_tut_burial_artifact.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabaster","wikidata":"Q143447"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Septimius_Severus_busto-Musei_Capitolini.jpg/500px-Septimius_Severus_busto-Musei_Capitolini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Septimius_Severus_busto-Musei_Capitolini.jpg/500px-Septimius_Severus_busto-Musei_Capitolini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alabaster artefact: A composite bust of the Emperor Septimius Severus; the head is marble and the bust is alabaster.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeptimius_Severus_busto-Musei_Capitolini.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/MorellaSantaMariaWindow.jpg/500px-MorellaSantaMariaWindow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/MorellaSantaMariaWindow.jpg/1280px-MorellaSantaMariaWindow.jpg?utm_source=en